        "Dev notes"
      ],
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Rust Foundation guest post (Victor Ciura, 10 Sep): Rust now has Tier-1 internal engineering status at Microsoft alongside C++, C#, and TypeScript.",
          "sourceIndexes": [
            0
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Tier-1 means a paved path to production: secure toolchain builds, tooling, quality workflows, platform integration, and SDL compliance.",
          "sourceIndexes": [
            0
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Centerpiece: rustc_codegen_utc — a rustc backend wired to MSVC’s UTC codegen (peer to LLVM/GCC/Cranelift backends) for Windows ABI, hardening, Hotpatch, and Rust/C++ interop.",
          "sourceIndexes": [
            0
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Production-ready since early 2026; self-hosted since Rust 1.90; >100 Microsoft repos already build with it.",
          "sourceIndexes": [
            0
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "HN front page overnight (~643 points) on the Foundation post.",
          "sourceIndexes": [
            1
          ]
        }
      ],
      "whyItMatters": "Memory-safe systems code gets the same Windows-native paved path as C++ — a structural signal for firmware, drivers, and hybrid stacks.",
