      "id": "forgejo-rce-patch",
      "title": "Forgejo 16.0.4 / 15.0.8: critical template RCE (CVE-2026-89094)",
      "topics": [
        "Security"
      ],
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Forgejo security advisory #59: v16.0.4 and v15.0.8 (LTS) fix a critical RCE in repo-from-template generation.",
          "sourceIndexes": [
            0
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Malicious `.forgejo/template` expansion could recreate a `.git` dir during init, letting attackers read host data and run processes (CVE-2026-89094, CVSS 9.9).",
          "sourceIndexes": [
            0,
            1
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Same releases also close an API auth bypass around “allow maintainer edits” with restricted tokens.",
          "sourceIndexes": [
            0
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Project: upgrade ASAP; Lobsters flagged the critical fix overnight.",
          "sourceIndexes": [
            2
          ]
        }
      ],
      "whyItMatters": "Self-hosted Git forges that accept template repos need this patch before the next “new repo from template” click.",
      "image": {
